;; F, the Low Door. The slab leans against the west wall; the hollow in the
;; roof is the place it once closed. Easy floor, E to G (rows 7-8). Over
;; the floor (11-12, row 6), the slab's old seat, a held jump up.
(room
  region: underhum
  at: (5 5)
  title: "The Low Door"
  intent: "a great slab leans against the wall where it once closed the bowl, and you walk under its place: a breath"
  bed: (hum 0.6 air 0.4 water 0.1)
  light: 0.2
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "##########    ###########"
   "########       ##########"
   "######           ########"
   "####                #####"
   "##                    ###"
   "#          ##           #"
   "                         "
   "                         "
   "#########################"
   "#########################")
  things: ((slab at: (4 8)))
  decor: none)
